why_we_need_this:
During a meeting, people refer to past agreements («мы же в прошлый раз договорились…») and nobody remembers the details. The copilot catches those moments and shows the matching note or task from the chosen PraxisOS project. Research AUG-196 measured that local search alone finds almost nothing on Russian meetings against English notes. With Claude (Sonnet) it found the real note in about 2–10 s for about $0.10–0.20 per meeting hour.

The user decided (2026-11-05):
- a four-position mode switch, default Off, with Claude explains marked recommended;
- choosing a Claude mode is the consent;
- model Haiku / Sonnet / Opus, default Sonnet, changeable during the meeting;
- Always-on only after a confirmation and with a per-meeting spending limit;
- Compact Mode: Dock Strip gets the side drawer (A3), Ghost Caption gets the floating card (B3).

Spec: @docs/mockups/AUG-196/findings.md. Mockups: @docs/mockups/AUG-196/copilot-hints.html (final) and @docs/mockups/AUG-196/compact-assistant.html (options A3 and B3). Background: @project-context/ai-assistants/README.md.

acceptance_criteria:
- [ ] LiveFeed per liveKey (server/src/services/liveFeed.ts), exactly as findings.md §5:
  - acquire/release refcount, ring buffer of 20 min / 6,000 words, never persisted;
  - push after the transcript send in liveTranscription.ts and correct() in the corrector callback;
  - created only when a copilot mode is not Off or the Active session is enabled;
  - LiveTextCorrector and LiveActionItemsExtractor behave exactly as before (their existing tests pass).
- [ ] Gate g2, a pure function with unit tests on ru/en samples:
  - the stem triggers from findings.md §1, with reflexive `договорил(ись|ась|ся)` only, plus task ids; no Latin-capital and no quoted rule;
  - over the lines of findings §1, it fires on all 15 true references and none of the 3 listed false ones, and fires 0 times on the game-video sample.
- [ ] Keyword builder:
  - task id, then project-lexicon terms (route names, "Also known as" entries, CamelCase/UPPER terms; fuzzy Latin match with edit distance ≤ 2), then ≤ 2 content words; ≤ 4 in total;
  - local search = search_project_context + find_task_by_keywords in parallel over Praxis MCP HTTP, 2 s timeout.
- [ ] copilotEngine per (liveKey, project):
  - limits: ≥ 20 s between searches, ≤ 1 card per route per 5 min, ≤ 12 Claude turns per hour, dedupe by route+line;
  - when PraxisOS is unreachable it sends copilot-status praxis-off and retries health every 30 s;
  - Local mode shows a card only on an [exact] or task hit; nothing found = no card, only the silent counter grows.
- [ ] Claude explains — a dedicated copilot child per (liveKey, project), separate from the Active session chat child:
  - flags, payload (≤ 80 words of trigger lines + ≤ 3 candidates) and prompt exactly as findings §3;
  - one-line JSON answer;
  - timeout 6 s with candidates (explain) and 12 s without (assist); on timeout or error it falls back to a plain card when a local hit exists, otherwise nothing is shown;
  - lazy spawn, idle stop after 10 min, stop on End Meeting, counted in AI_MAX_SESSIONS = 3.
- [ ] Always-on Claude per findings §4:
  - 30 s batches of ≥ 40 new words, child restart every 30 turns with a ≤ 150-word summary;
  - --max-budget-usd = aiCopilotAlwaysBudgetUsd (default 2); at the limit it switches this meeting to Claude explains with the status "Spending limit reached — switched to Claude explains";
  - switching it off mid-meeting stops the child within 5 s (taskkill /T /F on Windows).
- [ ] Preferences and routes per findings §2:
  - aiCopilotMode (off|local|claude|always, default off) and aiCopilotModel (haiku|sonnet|opus, default sonnet) are sanitized;
  - aiCopilotAlwaysBudgetUsd 0.5–10 step 0.5;
  - aiCopilotConsent / aiCopilotAlwaysAck are written only by POST /api/assistant/copilot-mode (not in ALLOWED_KEYS);
  - all defaults off, so with Off there is no LiveFeed, no MCP connection, no child and no new frame.
- [ ] WebSocket frames copilot-hint (states searching | found | explained | removed, upgraded in place by hintId), copilot-status, copilot-dismiss (suppresses the route or task for the rest of the meeting) and copilot-mode (change mode and model on the fly).
- [ ] UI matches @docs/mockups/AUG-196/copilot-hints.html:
  - ASSISTANT overlay Hints block in all 7 states;
  - CTX n badge next to the REC timer;
  - mode + model selects in the panel strip;
  - Settings → AI assistants copilot radio list with the price/privacy lines and the Always-on confirmation modal (checkbox-gated);
  - no model names, prices or token counts inside hint cards.
- [ ] Compact Mode matches @docs/mockups/AUG-196/compact-assistant.html:
  - A3: Dock Strip [ ◧ ] side drawer, 320 px to the left, window widens to 660 px through the shell on both platforms;
  - B3: Ghost Caption floating card 340 × ≤ 260 px above the caption's right end, fades to a CTX n chip after 20 s, not click-through while hovered;
  - Dock Square and Ghost Coin show the CTX n badge and switch to the transcript widget with the assistant open.
- [ ] Logs carry counts, timings, verdicts and costs only — never transcript text or keywords.
- [ ] Verified on Windows x64 and macOS arm64:
  - one live meeting per mode;
  - the mode switched mid-meeting;
  - the Always-on limit reached with a small test limit;
  - typecheck and the existing test suites green.
